; back to back, len = payload byte count (NOT interpreter A/B's whole-record
; count); op 0xFF is a 2-byte section terminator.  Walking this rule over the
; whole span lands exactly on the 672-byte 0x00 pad that runs to the physical
; end of the EPROM -- zero drift across 413 steps.  64 of the records (op
; 0x00-0x3F, each exactly once) are a uniform 32-byte SLOT TABLE; the rest are
; one-off records.  Field semantics are deferred; every byte is placed inside
; a record whose framing is proven, not left as an unexplained `.byte` run.
; Full proof: notes/gen_prom_b_f3f400_module.py.
; ==============================================================================

